thunder-mermaid
===============

The Rust sources in src/ are derived from `codex-rs/mermaid` in
https://github.com/openai/codex (Apache License 2.0).

Modifications:
  * crate manifest added (upstream lives in a workspace);
  * the upstream insta-based snapshot test modules were dropped, because they
    need `insta`/`pretty_assertions` and their snapshots are not vendored;
  * let-chains in `output.rs` and `relations.rs` were rewritten as equivalent
    `match`/`if let`, so the crate builds on our edition and MSRV;
  * `is_none_or` in `parse.rs` was rewritten as `matches!`, for the same reason;
  * `Shape::Rounded` and `Shape::Cylinder` were added so `A(label)` and
    `A[(label)]` parse. The upstream prototype only accepted `[]`, `{}` and
    `([ ])`, which rejected most real diagrams. They reuse the existing
    rounded-corner drawing arm; the layout algorithm is untouched.

The rendering algorithm, its bounds, and its public API are otherwise unchanged.

